# `words.jsonl` is one row per (cell, word) and runs ~80 MB over the full
# corpus -- 302 items x 8 pairs x ~100 moved words. It is REGENERATED by
# `run.py` from the store in minutes and nothing depends on the committed copy,
# so it is derived data at a size git should not carry.
#
# `cells.jsonl` (~3 MB) and `skipped.jsonl` ARE committed: they are the results
# proper, and `skipped.jsonl` in particular is the record of what was NOT
# measured and why, which cannot be reconstructed from a later run against a
# different population.
words.jsonl
